O","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7bb4619df617a3a739c0752d62b91c4c9b05b9b4.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7bb4619df617a3a739c0752d62b91c4c9b05b9b4.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch issued September 5 at 5:01PM MDT until September 5 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"THE NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE HAS ISSUED SEVERE THUNDERSTORM WATCH\n659 IN EFFECT UNTIL 9 PM MDT THIS EVENING FOR THE FOLLOWING AREAS\n\nIN COLORADO THIS WATCH INCLUDES 3 COUNTIES\n\nIN NORTHEAST COLORADO\n\nLOGAN                 PHILLIPS              SEDGWICK\n\nTHIS INCLUDES THE CITIES OF HOLYOKE, JULESBURG, AND STERLING.","ends":"2026-09-05T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Logan, CO; Phillips, CO; Sedgwick, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6aa6db82df20a8e40f1400ed99c679ac9ae0ffeb.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6aa6db82df20a8e40f1400ed99c679ac9ae0ffeb.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued September 5 at 4:31PM MDT until September 6 at 3:00AM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of northeast Colorado, including the following\ncounties, Logan County, Phillips County and Sedgwick County.\n\n* WHEN...Until 3 AM MDT Sunday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Scattered to numerous thunderstorms are expected to repeatedly\nmove across far northeast Colorado this evening and into the\nearly morning hours. Locally, up to 3 to 5 inches of rainfall is\npossible.","ends":"2026-09-06T03:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Logan County; Sedgwick County; Phillips County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6974fe397cb7c06998ee1635c046b5ec68211df3.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6974fe397cb7c06998ee1635c046b